{"MECHANISM_ID":"O-1","SOURCE_PROJECT":"orca-cli/orca","SOURCE_COMMIT":"5beeefcb57555962bb93facc54b5f82484731802","LICENSE":"MIT","PROBLEM":"Workers lose all in-flight execution state when the agent session compacts, dies, or is killed; the coordinator tracks attempts conversationally and reconstruction is manual.","MECHANISM":"Durable run row: UUIDv7 id, typed status, prompt, worktree_path, adapter, branch, started/completed timestamps in SQLite; single writer (SetMaxOpenConns(1)), WAL mode, busy_timeout, foreign keys on; status changes via UpdateStatus with updated_at bump.","INVARIANT":"Every unit of agent execution has exactly one durable identity row before it starts; status transitions are the only mutation path.","FAILURE_MODEL":"Process death mid-run leaves row in running state (no heartbeat/lease yet); DB file corruption loses local state (no replication); concurrent writers serialized by single-conn pool.","SECURITY_MODEL":"Local file; no auth layer; any process with file access can mutate runs.","SCALING_MODEL":"Single SQLite file; fine to thousands of runs; FTS5 keeps log search fast; no multi-machine story.","CRX_ANALOG":"MissionRuntime missions (idempotent deterministic IDs) exist; durable per-attempt Run identity is a proven gap (crx-audit gap #3). JSONL run ledgers exist but are not queryable state.","SEMANTIC_DELTA":"Orca's unit is the attempt (worker+worktree+lifecycle); CRX's unit is the mission. Orca rows survive worker death; CRX mission state lives in coordinator context.","HARVEST_CLASS":"ADAPT","INTEGRATION_COST":"Low: schema plus store methods; implement as run-scoped namespace of the canonical PG event journal, not a second SQLite writer.","EXPECTED_VALUE":"High: closes proven gap #3; makes workers disposable; prerequisite for rehydration protocol and interruption experiments.","FALSIFICATION_TEST":"Kill a worker mid-run; a fresh worker must reconstruct run identity, status, and worktree from durable state alone with no coordinator explanation."}
{"MECHANISM_ID":"O-2","SOURCE_PROJECT":"orca-cli/orca","SOURCE_COMMIT":"5beeefcb57555962bb93facc54b5f82484731802","LICENSE":"MIT","PROBLEM":"Run lifecycle transitions scattered through imperative code admit illegal states (e.g. ship from queued) that tests cannot enumerate.","MECHANISM":"Pure transition table: map[Status]map[Event]Status; Apply(from, event) is total, side-effect-free, returns ErrIllegalTransition for undefined pairs. Statuses: queued/pending/running/blocked/ready/failed/shipped/killed.","INVARIANT":"No transition exists unless it is a cell in the table; the table is the complete specification.","FAILURE_MODEL":"Table omissions are silent (a missing legal transition is a feature gap, not a crash); table is not enforced at the DB layer (status column is TEXT).","SECURITY_MODEL":"None; it is a pure function.","SCALING_MODEL":"O(1); irrelevant to scale.","CRX_ANALOG":"Typed failure semantics as doctrine (SOUL.md 11); verdict-authority admission checks; transitions embedded in runtime code.","SEMANTIC_DELTA":"Orca makes the lifecycle a declarative artifact; CRX keeps it procedural.","HARVEST_CLASS":"ADAPT","INTEGRATION_COST":"Very low: extract run/mission lifecycle transitions into tables; runtime calls the table.","EXPECTED_VALUE":"Medium: eliminates a class of illegal-state bugs; makes lifecycle reviewable as data.","FALSIFICATION_TEST":"Attempt every (status, event) pair; assert exactly the table's cells succeed and all others return ErrIllegalTransition."}
{"MECHANISM_ID":"O-3","SOURCE_PROJECT":"orca-cli/orca","SOURCE_COMMIT":"5beeefcb57555962bb93facc54b5f82484731802","LICENSE":"MIT","PROBLEM":"Parallel agents editing the same checkout collide; ad-hoc worktree management leaves orphaned worktrees and stale git registry entries.","MECHANISM":"CreateForRun: git worktree add -b orca/<runID> at .orca/runs/<runID>/ off base branch; ErrEmptyBase guard; symlink-resolved repo root. Archive: os.Rename to .orca/runs/_<kind>/<runID>/ (data preserved first), then git worktree prune; kind in {shipped,killed}.","INVARIANT":"One run owns exactly one worktree on exactly one branch; archival never destroys data before unregistering.","FAILURE_MODEL":"os.Rename across filesystems fails (same-repo assumption); prune failure leaves stale registry entry (non-fatal, retried next prune).","SECURITY_MODEL":"None beyond filesystem perms; worktree inherits repo access.","SCALING_MODEL":"Bounded by git worktree overhead; tens of concurrent runs fine.","CRX_ANALOG":"Ad-hoc git worktrees (e.g. jev-surgical); no create/archive discipline; orphan cleanup manual.","SEMANTIC_DELTA":"Orca: worktree lifecycle as code with typed errors; CRX: manual convention.","HARVEST_CLASS":"REUSE","INTEGRATION_COST":"Very low: ~120 lines, tested, MIT; adapt paths to CRX conventions.","EXPECTED_VALUE":"Medium: boring correctness for the 50-investigation target; kills orphaned-worktree class of failures.","FALSIFICATION_TEST":"Create 10 runs, kill 3, ship 2; assert git worktree list shows exactly the 5 live ones and archived dirs hold all 10 data sets."}
{"MECHANISM_ID":"O-4","SOURCE_PROJECT":"orca-cli/orca","SOURCE_COMMIT":"5beeefcb57555962bb93facc54b5f82484731802","LICENSE":"MIT","PROBLEM":"Multi-step agent work has implicit ordering in coordinator prompts; nothing represents 'B is blocked on A' as queryable data.","MECHANISM":"run_dependencies table: (run_id, dep_id) composite PK, FK cascades; Pending status + Pickup event semantics in the state table (scheduler itself unimplemented).","INVARIANT":"Dependencies are data, not prompt text; a run is runnable iff all deps are in terminal-success states.","FAILURE_MODEL":"Cycles undetectable (no cycle check in schema); scheduler unimplemented so invariant unenforced at HEAD.","SECURITY_MODEL":"None; local data.","SCALING_MODEL":"DAG queries are recursive CTEs; fine to thousands of nodes.","CRX_ANALOG":"Causation/correlation lineage on ping_events; mission lifecycle events lack causation_id (gap #6); no task DAG or dependency gating.","SEMANTIC_DELTA":"Orca: explicit blocking edges as first-class data; CRX: lineage on events, nothing on tasks.","HARVEST_CLASS":"ADAPT","INTEGRATION_COST":"Low: edges table plus a pure ready-set query; do not import a scheduler.","EXPECTED_VALUE":"High for the autonomy ladder L4-L5: dependency gating is prerequisite for agents selecting next work.","FALSIFICATION_TEST":"Insert a 3-node chain; the ready-set query must return only the unblocked node; introduce a cycle and assert it is detected, not hung."}
{"MECHANISM_ID":"O-5","SOURCE_PROJECT":"orca-cli/orca","SOURCE_COMMIT":"5beeefcb57555962bb93facc54b5f82484731802","LICENSE":"MIT","PROBLEM":"Review outcomes are free text; downstream automation cannot branch on whether a reviewer said merge, abandon, or needs-review.","MECHANISM":"Adapter.Result.Decision enum: merge | abandon | needs_review, alongside Status (success/error/killed) and structured Error{code,message}. Adapter port: Launch/Validate/Handle/Result; registry with duplicate-registration and unknown-adapter errors.","INVARIANT":"Every completed agent execution terminates in exactly one (Status, Decision) pair.","FAILURE_MODEL":"Zero concrete adapters exist; the port is unproven against real CLIs.","SECURITY_MODEL":"Validate() is the intended pre-flight; no enforcement story.","SCALING_MODEL":"N/A (interface).","CRX_ANALOG":"WorkerRuntime + 6 canonical workers (deterministic, lineage-preserving); no typed review-outcome vocabulary.","SEMANTIC_DELTA":"Orca separates execution outcome (Status) from review recommendation (Decision); CRX has no such vocabulary.","HARVEST_CLASS":"PATTERN","INTEGRATION_COST":"Trivial: adopt the Decision vocabulary for review gates; do not adopt the adapter port (CRX workers are sovereign, not pluggable CLIs).","EXPECTED_VALUE":"Medium: typed review outcomes enable merge-gate automation.","FALSIFICATION_TEST":"A reviewer agent must emit a Decision for every review; the merge gate must reject any review artifact lacking one."}
{"MECHANISM_ID":"O-6","SOURCE_PROJECT":"orca-cli/orca","SOURCE_COMMIT":"5beeefcb57555962bb93facc54b5f82484731802","LICENSE":"MIT","PROBLEM":"Agent context compacts or the session dies; the replacement agent cannot re-establish in-flight work without the human re-explaining.","MECHANISM":"Design only (unimplemented): on every session start the agent calls orca_list_runs via MCP, surfaces active runs, and resumes from durable state; reinforced by a mandatory instruction snippet in the agent's persistent config file.","INVARIANT":"A worker never depends on conversational memory for continuity; durable state is the source of truth on (re)start.","FAILURE_MODEL":"Unimplemented, so no failure data; prompt-level enforcement is brittle (agents ignore instructions).","SECURITY_MODEL":"Read-only state query; must not grant write authority beyond the worker's own run.","SCALING_MODEL":"N/A.","CRX_ANALOG":"Compaction summaries, MEMORY.md, daily logs; coordinator re-briefs workers conversationally; no agent-invoked rehydration protocol.","SEMANTIC_DELTA":"Orca (design): rehydration is a worker-initiated protocol against durable state; CRX: rehydration is coordinator-initiated conversation.","HARVEST_CLASS":"PATTERN","INTEGRATION_COST":"Medium: needs O-1 run rows plus a bounded read-only query surface.","EXPECTED_VALUE":"High: this is the mechanism that makes workers truly disposable; prerequisite for interruption experiments.","FALSIFICATION_TEST":"Start a worker, kill its session mid-task, start a fresh worker with no briefing; it must recover run identity, open tasks, and last checkpoint from the query surface alone."}
{"MECHANISM_ID":"O-7","SOURCE_PROJECT":"orca-cli/orca","SOURCE_COMMIT":"5beeefcb57555962bb93facc54b5f82484731802","LICENSE":"MIT","PROBLEM":"Ship/merge gates live as code; their evaluations are not auditable as data and their outcomes do not enter the evidence trail.","MECHANISM":"constraints table (name, command, timeout_s, enabled per pod); ConstraintsPassed/Block typed events in the state machine gating running->ready. Engine unimplemented at HEAD.","INVARIANT":"No run reaches ready without every enabled constraint emitting pass; every gate evaluation is an event.","FAILURE_MODEL":"Unimplemented; command-based constraints are shell injection surface if built naively.","SECURITY_MODEL":"Constraint commands execute with the runner's privileges; needs sandboxing if built.","SCALING_MODEL":"N/A.","CRX_ANALOG":"BindingVerifier, verdict-authority admission, URL-safety gates; outcomes are booleans, not events; gates are code, not data.","SEMANTIC_DELTA":"Orca: gate as data + typed outcome event; CRX: gate as enforced code with boolean outcome.","HARVEST_CLASS":"ADAPT","INTEGRATION_COST":"Low: represent gates as named checks whose pass/fail becomes a canonical event; aligns with existing verdict-event practice.","EXPECTED_VALUE":"Medium: auditable gates; each block carries evidence.","FALSIFICATION_TEST":"Disable a constraint mid-run; the run must not reach ready; the Block event must name the failing constraint."}
{"MECHANISM_ID":"O-8","SOURCE_PROJECT":"orca-cli/orca","SOURCE_COMMIT":"5beeefcb57555962bb93facc54b5f82484731802","LICENSE":"MIT","PROBLEM":"Agent run logs are unstructured text streams; finding what a run did weeks later is grep-scale work.","MECHANISM":"logs table (run_id, level, message, created_at) plus FTS5 virtual tables with insert triggers keeping them in sync; runs_fts over prompts.","INVARIANT":"Every log line is attributed to a run and full-text searchable.","FAILURE_MODEL":"FTS5 triggers only sync on INSERT (no update/delete triggers); large log volumes bloat the single DB file.","SECURITY_MODEL":"Logs may contain secrets; no redaction story.","SCALING_MODEL":"FTS5 handles millions of rows; single-file bloat is the limit.","CRX_ANALOG":"Cron run history, runs.jsonl ledgers, per-lane evidence markdown; retrieval is file-grep.","SEMANTIC_DELTA":"Orca: logs as queryable data from birth; CRX: logs as files, evidence as prose.","HARVEST_CLASS":"WATCH","INTEGRATION_COST":"Low, but premature at current scale; revisit at 50-investigation scale.","EXPECTED_VALUE":"Medium-long-term: failure analysis and cross-run learning need searchable execution history.","FALSIFICATION_TEST":"After 100 runs, a query for a specific error string must return the exact runs and timestamps without filesystem grep."}
{"MECHANISM_ID":"O-9","SOURCE_PROJECT":"orca-cli/orca","SOURCE_COMMIT":"5beeefcb57555962bb93facc54b5f82484731802","LICENSE":"MIT","PROBLEM":"UUID run IDs are unusable in conversation and CLI; naive prefix matching is ambiguous.","MECHANISM":"ShortRef: run_<first8hex>; ResolveShortRef with ErrAmbiguousRef / ErrRefNotFound; schema comment documents non-uniqueness, ambiguity detected at query time.","INVARIANT":"A short ref resolves to at most one run or fails loudly; never silently picks.","FAILURE_MODEL":"8-hex collisions grow with run count (birthday bound ~2^32); acceptable for human-scale use.","SECURITY_MODEL":"None.","SCALING_MODEL":"LIKE-prefix query; indexed id column keeps it fast.","CRX_ANALOG":"None; run IDs are conversational.","SEMANTIC_DELTA":"Trivial.","HARVEST_CLASS":"WATCH","INTEGRATION_COST":"Trivial; only relevant once run rows exist.","EXPECTED_VALUE":"Low.","FALSIFICATION_TEST":"Two runs sharing an 8-hex prefix must produce ErrAmbiguousRef, never a silent pick."}
{"MECHANISM_ID":"O-10","SOURCE_PROJECT":"orca-cli/orca","SOURCE_COMMIT":"5beeefcb57555962bb93facc54b5f82484731802","LICENSE":"MIT","PROBLEM":"Random UUIDs fragment B-tree indexes and reveal nothing about ordering; coordinated ID issuance is a bottleneck.","MECHANISM":"UUIDv7 for run IDs: monotonic, B-tree-friendly, uncoordinated issuance via google/uuid.","INVARIANT":"IDs are unique and roughly time-ordered without coordination.","FAILURE_MODEL":"Clock regression can produce out-of-order IDs; not a correctness issue for identity.","SECURITY_MODEL":"IDs are unguessable; no auth semantics.","SCALING_MODEL":"Ideal for indexed stores.","CRX_ANALOG":"IdentityAuthority doctrine: identity generation is sovereign; no prescribed UUID version.","SEMANTIC_DELTA":"Compatible, not competing.","HARVEST_CLASS":"PATTERN","INTEGRATION_COST":"Trivial, subject to IdentityAuthority approval.","EXPECTED_VALUE":"Low-medium: right default if CRX mints run IDs.","FALSIFICATION_TEST":"Generate 1M IDs across processes; assert uniqueness and monotonic ordering within a process."}
